Usage: hh_client check [OPTION]... [WWW-ROOT]

WWW-ROOT is assumed to be current directory if unspecified

Modes (mutually exclusive; choose one; default: --status):

  --find-class-refs        finds references of the provided class name
  --find-refs              finds references of the provided symbol; optionally specify the symbol kind like "Kind|Symbol" (looks for functions or methods if unspecified); valid kinds are Method, Property, Class_const, Typeconst, Function, Class, ExplicitClass, and GConst; use ExplicitClass instead of Class to exclude references via self/static/parent
  --identify               identify the named symbol
  --inheritance-ancestors  prints a list of all related classes or methods to the given class
  --inheritance-children   prints a list of all related classes or methods to the given class
  --list-files             list files with errors
  --outline                prints an outline of the text on stdin
  --outline-for-agents     <file> outline the file, including line spans, to help agents efficiently navigate large files
  --status                 show a human readable list of errors (default)
  --version                show version and exit

Options:

  --error-format <format> Error formatting style (default: highlighted); valid formats: agent, extended, raw, context, highlighted, plain, plain_highlighted
  --from                  so we know who's calling hh_client - e.g. nuclide, vim, emacs, vscode
  --json                  output json for machine consumption (default: false)
  --jsonl                 output streaming jsonl (JSON Lines) for machine consumption (default: false)
  --max-errors            Maximum number of errors to display
  --preexisting-warnings  show all preexisting warnings in typechecked files (default: false)
  --reason                reason for invoking hh, logged to telemetry
  --single <path>         Return errors in file with provided name (give '-' for stdin)
  --multi <path>          Return errors for files read from the given file (one per line)
  --timeout               set the timeout in seconds (default: no timeout)
  -Wall                   show all warnings
  -Wnone                  hide all warnings
  -W                      show all warnings with a given code, e.g. -W 12001
  -Wno                    hide all warnings with a given code, e.g. -Wno 12001
  -Wignore-files          hide warnings in files matching a regexp
  -Wgenerated             show warnings in generated files
  --ultrahelp             see all modes and options, including less frequently used ones
  -help                   Display this list of options
  --help                  Display this list of options
